INT. GRANDMOTHER'S ATTIC - EARLY EVENING

Slanted beams. Trunks and a dress form wearing a wedding veil. A single dormer window lets in orange light.

ODALYS FERREIRA (8) clutches a flashlight like a sword. She crouches behind a trunk. Her brother, RUBEN (11), hunches beside her, whispering. Her cousin, ISAURA (13), perches on the dress form's stand, bored. They are hiding.

Down the stairs, a door bangs. Heavy footsteps.

She presses a finger to her lips. He nods. Isaura rolls her eyes but goes quiet.

A shape fills the stairwell. GRANDMOTHER FERREIRA (70s, flowered apron, spoon in hand) climbs into view, scanning the room. She frowns.

GRANDMOTHER
Odalys? Ruben? Isaura? Dinner!

ODALYS
(whispering)
Shh.

RUBEN
You shh.

ISAURA
You're both shh.

GRANDMOTHER
I heard that.

Nobody moves. The old woman steps closer to the trunk. She reaches down, grips the lid.

She throws it open. Odalys shrieks. Ruben yelps. Isaura topples off the stand, veil flying.

GRANDMOTHER (CONT'D)
Found you!

They stare at her. Then, all at once, they burst out laughing, breathless and relieved.

ODALYS
That's not fair, you cheated!

GRANDMOTHER
Old ladies are allowed.

Tension gone, she ladles a spoonful of soup into Odalys's mouth. Odalys swallows, grinning.

UNCLE TOMAS (O.S.)
Is that my mother screaming up there?

He thunders up the stairs, and everyone starts shouting at once.
